le multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the observable sink for the phase metrics (structured metric field / log key / artifact) and add an assertion that a test emits and checks it (e.g. jq -e '.metrics.lock_hold_ms' on the emitted record).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 7: 'Measure ticket-OID capture, lazy reads/reduction, receipt validation, bundle preparation, lock wait/hold, local commit, and push/retry.'","The CI-tests AC lists 'focused lazy-read parity, hierarchy/link phantom, negative-read, resolver, cross-process concurrency, and rollback tests' but does not include a metric-emission assertion.","ABSENCE: no named metric/log key or artifact schema the test asserts against."],"finding":"The metrics acceptance criterion ('wait/hold are measured') and step 7 name the phases to measure but do not specify the observable sink (structured metric field, log key, or emitted artifact) that a CI test can assert on, so no proving command produces evidence that the phase timings are actually emitted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcf1bcc9a24980c73","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC line 'LLM work, lazy reads, receipt validation, preparation, and push occur outside the write lock ... wait/hold are measured'; Step 7","norm_id":"n1c226e470e4449c0","priority":0.0611,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer wants to confirm lock wait/hold is instrumented, but no test asserts the emitted timing field exists."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define a RETIRE/cleanup path for the OID/schema-keyed derived caches (eviction bound, TTL, or GC on schema change / unreachable OID) so they do not accumulate unbounded.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Put derived resolver/graph indexes outside the immutable tree and key them by tracker OID plus schema version.'","'Derived caches are OID/schema-keyed with per-run temporaries and do not write inside the pinned view.'","ABSENCE: no eviction, TTL, LRU bound, or GC-on-schema-change is stated for the OID-keyed cache set."],"finding":"The derived resolver/graph indexes are keyed by tracker OID plus schema version and written outside the immutable tree, but the plan never defines a RETIRE/cleanup/eviction path. Each new tracker OID (every normal write advances the tracker) creates a fresh cache entry, so these derived caches accumulate unbounded over the life of the store.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f70ec0c2521a5635c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 / Acceptance Criteria 'Derived caches are OID/schema-keyed with per-run temporaries'","norm_id":"n65fda7a860927871","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A long-running dogfood store advances the tracker OID on every write; the derived resolver/graph cache directory grows one entry per OID indefinitely, consuming disk with no reclamation.","A schema-version bump orphans all prior-schema cache entries with no defined path to remove them."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a bounded/evictable cache policy (e.g. LRU by OID or prune entries whose tracker OID is no longer reachable, and drop entries on schema-version change) and state where/when cleanup runs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly in the Contract/receipt vocabulary that receipt validation keys only on reducer-visible (state-bearing) inputs and excludes operation-owned observability sidecars (e.g. reducer-ignored COMPLETION_VERDICT), so a close never conflicts with its own sidecar write.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Research comment: 'A raw target-tree dependency would make completion conflict with its own sidecar write. Validation must distinguish state-bearing inputs from operation-owned observability events, or validate before any sidecar write and carry the result atomically into mutation.'","Plan step 3 validates 'the receipt from A against current descendant Tn' and diffs 'changed ticket/global paths' without naming the reducer-ignored/observability exclusion.","Code confirms COMPLETION_VERDICT is reducer-IGNORED (src/rebar/reducer/_version.py, src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py) so the exclusion is implicitly available but not stated in the plan."],"finding":"The plan's receipt-validation mechanism does not explicitly carry forward the research's self-write distinction (state-bearing inputs vs. operation-owned observability events), which is load-bearing for correctness: a validator that keys a receipt on the raw ticket-tree OID would conflict with the operation's own COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar write and never converge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f87e9902618bcf425","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Contract (ticket view / receipt) and Plan step 3/5","norm_id":"ndc79fcb8913131b4","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A relevant-delta validator recomputes affected predicates and includes the just-written PASS sidecar path in the diff, treating the operation's own artifact as a conflicting mutation and forcing an infinite restart-at-Tn loop."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Contract's receipt clause (and step 3), add that read receipts and delta-diff validation are computed over reducer-visible state only; operation-owned observability events such as the reducer-ignored COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar are excluded from state-bearing dependencies, matching the research self-write finding.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concurrency model as snapshot-isolation + optimistic-concurrency-control (citing the established SI/OCC prior art and comparable git-as-database systems), map the plan's conflict classes (exact/hierarchy/link/negative/resolver) onto the standard anomaly taxonomy, and state explicitly which invariants the both-endpoints predicate revalidation guarantees vs. the residual snapshot-isolation write-skew/phantom boundary.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7623,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan pins a read basis at tickets_oid, prepares work outside the lock, asserts 'tracker HEAD still equals validated Tn' inside the lock, and on push rejection does 'fetch and revalidate ... restart verification' (steps 4-6) — the canonical MVCC snapshot-isolation + optimistic-concurrency-control loop.","Retrieved prior art (sjhwangwiki.com MVCC/SI; DDIA ch.7 via 91dfj.org) documents this exact pattern and its classic anomaly: 'Snapshot isolation ... is not the same as serializability. The classic anomaly is write skew, where two transactions read the same snapshot, update different rows, and jointly violate an invariant.'","The plan enumerates conflict classes ('exact, hierarchy, link, negative, or resolver conflict') ad hoc rather than referencing the standard conflict/anomaly taxonomy that names phantoms and write skew explicitly.","Established git-as-database systems (Dolt, Datomic, Irmin) implement this OID-pinned-read + optimistic-commit model; the plan does not acknowledge them as prior art."],"finding":"The concurrency/atomicity design is a snapshot-isolation + optimistic-concurrency-control scheme over a Git-versioned object store, but the plan neither names that established prior art nor frames its ad-hoc conflict-class taxonomy against it, and does not state the known snapshot-isolation write-skew/phantom boundary its predicate-revalidation is meant to close.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f805ae97780b4cabe","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 3-6; Contract ('one stable read basis and one atomic publication boundary')","norm_id":"nc8d2cfcf2760a2c4","priority":0.0377,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer or future maintainer cannot tell whether the revalidation set is complete without a reference model, risking a missed anomaly class (e.g., a write-skew invariant spanning two 'unrelated' tickets that both revalidate as valid).","Author re-derives conflict classes that a named SI/SSI model would have supplied off-the-shelf."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"18b6e1739287439a","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["41ebf029739c48a0",6861],"description_boxes":["ea156a2c16eb8f24",13],"file_impact":["c3c3f7eb6a9ebb1c",45],"ticket_id":["4078c6697df861f8",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4992.8,"input_tokens":1244723,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":361536.8,"output_tokens":27409,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":374299.9,"verify_requests":36},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"none","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthrop